      "problem": "If $-x+9=7$, then $x=${{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "First, we apply the addition principle, subtracting $9$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-x+9 & =7 \\\\ -x+9-9 & =7-9 \\\\ -x+0 & =-2 \\\\ -x & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSecond, we apply the multiplication principle. We multiply by $-1$ to get rid of the negative sign.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-x & =-2 \\\\ (-1)\\cdot (-x) & =(-1)\\cdot (-2) \\\\ x & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$",
